In article <19600@cfctech.UUCP> kevin@cfctech.UUCP (Kevin Darcy) writes:
>Please speak up if you have an opinion on this whole poly-pile issue...

Neon.Stanford.EDU is the main student machine of the CS department here
at Stanford.  The password file has 587 entries.  Many people play
nethack: the last place on the top 100 list has more than 5000 points,
and reached level 6.  However, only one person ascended to demigod-hood
without cheating.  I got pretty far legally (level 29), in games which
seemed like total winners, and always got killed by some sort of
stupidity or bad luck.  Just to see what winning is like, I played in
wizard mode once and realized how far I really was from winning:
Liches, Titans, the Wiz, 20 maze levels and a long journey back up,
plus a pretty tough endgame level (monsters with more than 100 HPs).

Is the game really that easy with a wand of polymorph?  I figure it
should still take many hours just to go through 48 levels or so.  Also,
I often find that the real problem is not getting stuff, but deciding
what to carry-- even with gauntlets of power and with real strength
18/30, a significant part of my carrying capacity is wasted on my armor
(I can't get very far unless my AC is -10 or so, and this usually
requires several pieces of armor).  Then there's also food and a few
pieces of weaponry and some gems to throw at unicorns and a mirror and
a blindfold and...  How can people still carry 6 amulets of save life
and more than two named weapons, plus several wands of wishing and
wands of polymorph?

My vote is *NOT* to restrict the polymorphing trick.  Those who feel
the game is too easy should play as healers, or tourists, for challenge
(maybe start over a few times until you get a weak enough character,
with initial strength 7 :-)  Try to get through the first few levels!

